                 WHAT THE PROVER REFUSED, kept on the record. The first claim
                 written for Score also said it never exceeds the SAMPLE list's
                 length. GNATprove could not discharge it, and it is false: if
                 the population list holds one key three times and the sample
                 holds it once, support is 3 and the score is 3, above the
                 sample's length of 1. Upstream's lists are duplicate-free by
                 construction (one substitution per genome coordinate), so the
                 bound holds there — but this core does not assume distinctness,
                 so it does not claim the bound. It was withdrawn from the
                 claim, not added as an assumption.

                 What IS proved: membership agrees with the quantified
                 statement; support never exceeds the population's length;
                 support and conflict_alt partition the population list exactly
                 (conflict_alt = length - support), and conflict_ref partitions
                 the sample list the same way from the other side; the score
                 never exceeds the support, never exceeds the population list's
                 length, and never falls below minus the two lengths together;
                 and when each list is wholly contained in the other, the score
                 is exactly the population list's length.

